 "description": "Say what a file is, in your own words. description is what it shows: on a base image, who is on camera \u2014 \"a woman in her early twenties, blonde hair in a loose bun\" \u2014 and a campaign reads it so the same person appears in every render instead of changing between them. tags are labels to filter by, like sound-effect; metadata is how it was made \u2014 provider, model, prompt, jobId, costUsd, sourceUrl, ref, inputs. Each replaces what is there: null clears a description or metadata, [] clears tags. purpose switches a file between library, to post, and source, raw material kept to reuse. For several files at once, items, up to 50: a file not recorded yet comes back in not_found, to save once media_list shows it. Nothing else about a file can be changed here; what it is was read from the file itself.",
